  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1240 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nExpect very warm to hot temperatures Sunday as the 500 MB heights \nare little lower and low level moisture is less during the \nafternoon(upper 50s to lower 60s). Highs will range from the low to \nmid 90s south, to 100 to 102 across the northwest Concho Valley and \nwestern half of the Big Country. Looks like a Heat Advisory will not \nbe needed. The upper level ridge will expand eastward by next week. \nThis will result in hotter temperatures returning, with Heat \nAdvisories likely for portions of the area once again. Please follow \nheat safety precautions if you have to be outside.",
